pSeek-fueled AI boom.</strong></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0"><li =
style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:2=
6px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;m=
argin:0"><span>The article starts with an anecdote: earlier this year, Zhan=
g Xun, a sales rep for Volcano Engine (Bytedance=E2=80=99s cloud offering),=
 worried about meeting his sales quotas. DeepSeek=E2=80=99s release, howeve=
r, </span><em>=E2=80=9Cdropped a bombshell in the market,=E2=80=9D</em><spa=
n> driving AI demand across industries and sending cloud usage soaring. As =
he put it: =E2=80=9C</span><em>GPUs flew off the shelves in the first half =
of the year.=E2=80=9D</em></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p sty=
le=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:borde=
r-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0">A surprising source of dema=
nd came from government agencies and state-owned enterprises, which at time=
s showed more enthusiasm for deploying DeepSeek than private firms.</p></li=
><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-hei=
